<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- SpotBugs project decisions: a rule, or a rule in part of the code, that the team has decided not
     to enforce. One Match per decision, with a comment giving the reason, for example:

       <!- - JPA entities share associations by design (reason ...) - ->
       <Match><Package name="~team\.projectpulse\..*"/><Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/></Match>

     Unlike the baseline, this file may grow, but every entry is a reviewed decision. -->
<FindBugsFilter>
    <!-- D1: EI_EXPOSE_REP and EI_EXPOSE_REP2 are off for the whole project.
         All 219 findings on 2026-11-01 were one of three shapes, and in none of them does the class
         own the object it was handed or hands out:
         1. JPA entity getters and setters for an association or a collection (Course.getSections(),
            Team.setSection(), ...). The entity graph is shared by design, and the code depends on the
            live collection: 17 call sites mutate through a getter, for example TeamService.transferStudent
            (from.getStudents().remove / to.getStudents().add) and Section.addInstructor
            (instructor.getSections().add). A defensive copy would make those writes silently vanish.
         2. Constructor injection of Spring singletons (EvaluationController(EvaluationService, ...)).
            Sharing the one bean instance is the point of dependency injection.
         3. Request/response DTO records and report POJOs, built and serialized within one request.
            EvaluationService.generateWeeklyPeerEvaluationReportForSection fills its report through
            report.getPeerEvaluationAverages().add(...), so a copying getter would return an empty report.
         Check: every EI entry deleted from spotbugs-baseline.xml names an @Entity, a Spring bean
         constructor, a record under a dto package, or a report/result POJO. -->
    <Match>
        <Or>
            <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/>
            <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
        </Or>
    </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
